# 🛡️ Kubernetes Pod Security Checklist

Before deploying a Pod, check:

```text
☑ Run as non-root
☑ Disable privilege escalation
☑ Drop unnecessary Linux capabilities
☑ Use read-only root filesystem
☑ Use seccomp
☑ Avoid privileged containers
☑ Avoid unnecessary hostNetwork/hostPID/hostIPC
☑ Avoid hostPath when possible
☑ Use dedicated ServiceAccounts
☑ Disable ServiceAccount token mounting when unnecessary
☑ Apply least-privilege RBAC
☑ Use NetworkPolicies
☑ Store credentials in Secrets / external secret managers
☑ Define CPU and memory requests/limits
☑ Configure liveness/readiness/startup probes
☑ Scan container images
☑ Use minimal and trusted base images
☑ Avoid mutable `latest` tags
☑ Consider image signing and verification
☑ Apply Pod Security Standards
☑ Keep Kubernetes and container images patched
```

